  "body": "Part of #2007.\n\nMaintainer in chat, 2026-11-15: \"That tool editor issue is a P3\".\n\n## What happens\n\n- `WorkMaterial` (`crates/tools/src/cutting.rs:60-67`) has 6 values and no `Unknown`.\n- A tool keeps one `rpm`/`feed` (`crates/tools/src/tools.rs:209-210`) as the fallback, and `cutting: Vec<CuttingRow>` (L239) with rpm and feed only. There is no stepdown and no stepover in a row.\n- `material_group` (L206) is free text.\n- The material is one value for the document (`WorkMaterialDef`, `crates/app/src/schema.rs:674-679`; `cutting::material_of`, `crates/app/src/cutting.rs:28`). The setup stock has no material.\n\n## What to do\n\n1. Add `WorkMaterial::Unknown` (word `unknown`). It is the default row of each tool.\n2. Add stepdown and stepover to `CuttingRow`. A missing value falls back to the `Unknown` row.\n3. Migration: on load, the old `rpm`/`feed` of a tool become its `Unknown` row. `PROJECT_VERSION` 61 to 62 (`crates/app/src/project/file.rs:97`). `.camtools` `VERSION` 1 to 2 (`crates/app/src/tool_library.rs:31-33`); the reader accepts 1 and migrates it.\n4. Add an optional material to the setup stock. The row is selected by the setup stock material, then the document material, then `Unknown`.\n5. Show a table of rows for each material in the Cutting data group of the tool page.\n6. Keep the law of `crates/app/src/cutting_rows.rs`: a row moves numbers only inside a command, never on load.\n\nThis changes the feeds and speeds that the post reads. It is `effort:high` by the safety floor. An older build refuses the new file: the PR is `feat!` with a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer.\n\n## Done means:\n\n- A tool has an `Unknown` row, and a new tool gets it.\n- A v61 project and a v1 `.camtools` file load with no loss. The old rpm/feed show as the `Unknown` row. A test pins this.\n- A setup stock material selects the row for the operations of that setup. A test pins the order: stock, then document, then `Unknown`.\n- Stepdown and stepover from the row seed an operation only inside an undoable command.\n- The posted S and F words do not change for a project with no new rows. A golden test pins this.\n- An MCP tool sets the stock material, or a `MCP: <command>` issue is filed.\n\nOrder: independent of the layout work. The table UI goes in the group from the layout sub-issue.\n",
